  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 217 PM CDT Mon Sep 7 2026\n\nRain chances will remain in the forecast every afternoon this week \nas the seabreeze moves westward. The best chances for these \nscattered seabreeze thunderstorms will be across the Coastal Plains \nand Brush Country. A mid-level disturbance will move across the \nregion mid-week promoting low to medium (20-60%) chances for showers \nand thunderstorms across the eastern half with the best across the \nVictoria Crossroads. The ample moisture and warm temperatures this \nweek will promote elevated hist risk conditions each day. Heat index \nvalues will be within 105-110 degrees each afternoon with a moderate \nto high risk of heat-related impacts. If working outdoors, make sure \nto take frequent breaks and hydrate adequately. \n\nMore heat safety information can be found at weather.gov/heat",
